### Marquez REST API playground.
### Works with the VS Code / Cursor "REST Client" extension (click "Send Request" above a request)
### or the JetBrains HTTP client. Each request is also a plain `curl` call.
### API docs: https://marquezproject.github.io/marquez/openapi.html
###
### Note: namespaces and dataset names contain ':' and '/' and must be URL-encoded in paths
###   postgres://localhost:5433  ->  postgres%3A%2F%2Flocalhost%3A5433
###   data/raw/orders.csv        ->  data%2Fraw%2Forders.csv
### nodeId query parameters may be left unencoded.

@api = http://localhost:9000/api/v1
@pg = postgres%3A%2F%2Flocalhost%3A5433
@files = file%3A%2F%2Fopenlineage-poc

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- basics
### Namespaces (one per producer/data source/job group)
GET {{api}}/namespaces

###
### Jobs in a namespace
GET {{api}}/namespaces/poc_python_pipeline/jobs

###
### Datasets in a namespace
GET {{api}}/namespaces/{{pg}}/datasets

###
### One dataset, including its facets and fields
GET {{api}}/namespaces/{{pg}}/datasets/warehouse.public.fct_daily_revenue

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- runs and versions
### Run history of a job (state, duration, run facets such as errorMessage / parent)
GET {{api}}/namespaces/poc_python_pipeline/jobs/daily_pipeline.clean_orders/runs

###
### Dataset versions: one per run that wrote the dataset - compare "fields" to spot schema changes
GET {{api}}/namespaces/{{files}}/datasets/data%2Fraw%2Forders.csv/versions

###
### Job versions (a new version is created when the job's inputs/outputs/SQL change)
GET {{api}}/namespaces/poc_raw_events/jobs/ingest_orders/versions

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- lineage graph
### Dataset-level lineage around a dataset (depth = hops in both directions)
GET {{api}}/lineage?nodeId=dataset:postgres://localhost:5433:warehouse.public.fct_daily_revenue&depth=5

###
### Same, starting from a job
GET {{api}}/lineage?nodeId=job:poc_python_pipeline:daily_pipeline.clean_orders&depth=3

###
### Column-level lineage: where does "revenue" come from? (upstream is the default)
GET {{api}}/column-lineage?nodeId=datasetField:file://openlineage-poc:data/marts/daily_revenue.csv:revenue&depth=5

###
### Column-level lineage downstream of a column (impact analysis).
### Quirk: for a column of a dataset that no job has produced with column lineage (e.g. a raw source), Marquez
### returns an empty graph here - start from a derived column such as stg_orders.amount, or merge the
### upstream graphs of all datasets locally (see explore.ipynb).
GET {{api}}/column-lineage?nodeId=datasetField:postgres://localhost:5433:warehouse.public.stg_orders:amount&depth=5&withDownstream=true

###
### Column lineage for a whole dataset
GET {{api}}/column-lineage?nodeId=dataset:postgres://localhost:5433:warehouse.public.stg_orders&depth=2

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- search and raw events
### Full-text search over jobs and datasets
GET {{api}}/search?q=orders&limit=10

###
### Raw events as stored (the same payloads you sent), newest first
GET {{api}}/events/lineage?limit=5

###
### Raw events within a time window
GET {{api}}/events/lineage?limit=5&after=2026-10-01T00:00:00Z&sortDirection=desc

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- metadata you can add
### Create a tag ...
PUT {{api}}/tags/PII
Content-Type: application/json

{ "description": "Personally identifiable information" }

###
### ... tag a dataset ...
POST {{api}}/namespaces/{{pg}}/datasets/warehouse.public.stg_customers/tags/PII

###
### ... or a single column (visible in the UI on the dataset page)
POST {{api}}/namespaces/{{pg}}/datasets/warehouse.public.stg_customers/fields/email/tags/PII

###
### Send an event yourself (same endpoint the clients use)
POST {{api}}/lineage
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventType": "COMPLETE",
  "eventTime": "2026-10-24T12:00:00.000Z",
  "producer": "https://example.com/manual",
  "schemaURL": "https://openlineage.io/spec/2-0-2/OpenLineage.json#/$defs/RunEvent",
  "run": { "runId": "11111111-2222-3333-4444-555555555555" },
  "job": { "namespace": "manual", "name": "hello_lineage" },
  "inputs": [{ "namespace": "manual", "name": "in_table" }],
  "outputs": [{ "namespace": "manual", "name": "out_table" }]
}
